                <pb facs="0424" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg326"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1067.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm on the overleaf the President’s
                    telegram of yesterday to His Majesty the German Emperor, relative to the murder
                    of the German minister at Pekin.</p>
                <p>The regret at Baron von Ketteler’s untimely end is keenly felt in this city,
                    where his long residence is most agreeably recalled by those with whom he held
                    official and social relations.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d388-a1.xml" xpointer="d388-a1"/>
